        void start();
        void accelerate(); // Voilation, it will throw error.
     }
    Common built in functioanl Interfaces:
       EX: Predicate<T>  -> test() -> returns boolean
       Function<T, R>   -> apply() -> takes input and returns output.
       BiFunction<M, T, R> -> apply() -> takes 2 input arguments and returns output.

 - Stream API
    It is a powerful API used to process sequence of elements like Collections or arrays.
    EX: Sorting, Summing of elements, filter only even elements, filter only odd items
     It has 3 steps:
       1. Source - Here data comes from Collections or arrays.
       2. Intermediate Operations - Sorting, filtering etc will come under Inter. operation.
       For this step the data will come from source.
       ex: sorted(), filter().
       Every time an intermediate operation is performed the by prodcut is stream again.
       3. ternary operation - this marks the end of stream. once this operation is applied 
       the stream cannot be used again.
       ex: forEach(), collect()

